Documentation for API for frontend to read

This is going to be the following data in the output. 

Artist ID | Neighbor ID | Recording ID | Synthetic (Bool)


The additional data for the frontend to lookup:
Artist: Artist Name 
Neighbor: Neighbor Name
Recording: Recording Name, Recording Popularity
Synthetic: 
   - If false, show link to track
   - If true, show the following data:
       - predicted connection strength (Logistic Regression Results)
       - predicted tracks (default 5, user can input more) (CVAE Model Results)
       - predicted popularity (Linear Regression)
       

If we get synthetic tracks we have to tell the backend to apply the models
Then we have to tell the frontend (okay we will run it, here are the results)

Frontend sends:
ArtistID | Non-existing NeighborID 

OR 

Frontend sends

ArtistID 
Then backend creates Non-existing NeighborID

Backend returns the synthetic data above

Frontend:

GET 
/lookup?name=?synth=False? -> Returns the neighbor from the lookup name

This is going to be our neighbors, we will put this into a table

GET
/synth/artists?src=?dst=?limit= -> This tells the backend: Find me synthetic connections for this src and this dst

GET
/synth/artists?src=?limit= -> This tells the backend: Find me synthetic dst for this src 

GET
/synth/tracks?src=?dst=?limit= -> This tells the backend: Find me synthetic tracks for the src-dst connections



Backend:
POST
/lookup?name? -> Already have this, this is our search function posting it's connections when it runs the search

src | dst | probability (Logit) | Existing Tracks

POST
/synth/artists?src=?dst=?limit= -> Backend will Return the following:

src | dst | probability (Results of Logistic Regression)

This is acheived by:
1. get_artist_embeddings(src) & get_artist_embeddings(dst)
   - This goes into the database, returns their embeddings
2. load_logit_model(model_id)
3. predict_links(logit_model,src,dst)

POST
/synth/artists?src=?limit= -> Backend needs to find connections for the src

src | dst | probability (Results of Logistic Regression)

1. get_artist_embeddings(src)
   - This goes into the database, returns their embeddings
2. load_logit_model(model_id)
3. predict_links(logit_model,src)
4. get_artist_predictions(src)
   - Returns a table of predicted connections


POST
/synth/tracks?src=?dst=?limit= -> Backend will run the CVAE model by putting in the embeddings of the two artists

src | dst | probability (Logit) | Synthetic Track Features (CVAE)| Popularity (Linear Regression) 

1. get_artist_embeddings(src) & get_artist_embeddings(dst)
   - This goes into the database, returns their embeddings
2. GET /synth/artist?src=?dst=?
3. load_cvae_artifact(path)
4. generate_for_rows([(src,dst])

Returns Parquet of the table above





































